WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.799
Speaker 1: We have just insane news.

00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:12.250
News Corp Slack's Fox News is going to be
launching their own Weather Channel, if you

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.290
can believe it.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:20.120
The week is reporting that Fox is launching
a weather streaming service and it is already

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.980
feuding with the Weather Channel.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:28.030
Rupert Murdoch is looking to rain on the Weather
Channel's parade.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:29.789
There's there's a nice line.

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:35.929
Murdoch is set to debut a new streaming service,
FOX, whether this fall with his company believing

00:00:35.929 --> 00:00:41.780
that the, quote, sometimes staid world of
weather TV is ripe for disruption.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:46.320
The New York Times reports FOX weather is
aiming to take on the Weather Channel, but

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.719
the Times noted that the latter company is
already throwing some shade at its new competitor.

00:00:51.719 --> 00:00:55.420
Weather Channel chief content officer Naura
Zimet told The New York Times they couldn't

00:00:55.420 --> 00:01:00.519
even get a headline headline right about Tropical
Storm Bill slamming a recent article on Fox

00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:03.949
News's website claiming the storm posed a
massive threat.

00:01:03.949 --> 00:01:09.070
I applaud Fox getting into the weather space,
but they should really leave the saving information

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.010
to the experts.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.549
That is not really the issue for me.

00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:16.460
The issue for me is the next aspect of this
that's addressed.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.310
Zimet added that climate change is too important
to politicize and if they do that, they will

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.430
be doing Americans a disservice.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:28.160
A Fox weather spokesperson pushed back, telling
the Times, quote, While the Weather Channel

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:34.399
is focused on trolling Fox News.com for unrelated
stories, Fox Weather is busy preparing the

00:01:34.399 --> 00:01:40.649
debut of our innovative platform to deliver
critical coverage to an incredibly underserved

00:01:40.649 --> 00:01:41.859
market.

00:01:41.859 --> 00:01:49.659
When I hear that Fox weather says weather
is an underserved market, when it's a third

00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:55.969
of the nightly local news on the 6:00 p.m.
news and basically every market on the 11:00

00:01:55.969 --> 00:02:01.130
p.m. news and basically every market, if you
look at a half hour of local news, those those

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:07.229
half hour news shows, once you take out commercials,
it's twenty one minutes, often six or seven

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:11.650
of those twenty one minutes are weather a
third on.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:17.000
And in addition to that, you have the Weather
Channel, in addition to that, everybody on

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.110
their phones has constant live weather.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:25.130
And when there are notable weather events,
the major cable networks like MSNBC, CNN and

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:26.390
Fox cover weather.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:33.020
So when I hear Fox weather say that weather
is underserved, what I'm hearing is there's

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:40.280
not enough climate denial, presented a science
and and packaged as if it is the Weather Channel.

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:44.080
And that is what I fundamentally believe that
this is about.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:53.310
They make billions by playing political theater,
stoking polarization, stoking gridlock, allowing

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:57.890
the people who say Trump really won and all
of this stuff to just appear on their network,

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:03.170
they build that up and then they build themselves
up as the ones who will tell you the truth.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:06.850
Why am I not seeing on the other networks
that Trump actually won?

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:09.220
Well, maybe it's because Trump didn't really
win.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:12.470
No, it's because nobody but Fox will tell
me the truth.

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:19.440
That's the ideology and the attitude that
they sort of stoke in their audience and with

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.840
a fair amount of climate denial.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:21.840
Right.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:26.570
Remember the clips from Fox News, despite
it being bitterly cold in the winter in North

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:31.400
Dakota, in D.C., Democrats are talking about
climate change, those types of headlines.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.690
So they've got the perfect audience for it.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:37.770
And now they will smoothly make the switch
and say, hey, we'll also tell you the truth

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:42.600
